(B) Minus-sheet Syracuse offset: Syr_b^n(N) = 3^n 2^{-|a|} N + b F_n(a)
==============================================================================
offset identity verified for both signs, odd N < 16384, n <= 6: 98304 instances
valuation words with |a| <= 12: 4095 words, counts identical on both sheets,
   every word (a_1..a_n) realised by exactly 2^(13-|a|) odd N in [1, 2^14)
   => the word law is exactly Geom(2)^n truncated at |a| <= J on both sheets
Corollary: Syrac_-(Z/3^nZ) = -Syrac_+(Z/3^nZ) as random variables mod 3^n,
   and dTV(-X, -X + Unif(3^m Z/3^n Z)) = dTV(X, X + Unif(3^m Z/3^n Z)).
n = 3, |a| <= 12: the minus-sheet offset residue histogram mod 27 is the negation of the plus-sheet one (checked, 18 residues hit, multiples of 3 hit: 0)

